    "result": "Perfect! The implementation is complete. Let me create a final verification summary:\n\n## Implementation Complete \u2713\n\nI've successfully implemented the threshold feature for `frai eval` to gate CI jobs on evaluation metric scores. Here's what was added:\n\n### **Core Changes**\n\n1. **CLI (`frai-cli/src/index.ts`)**\n   - Added `--threshold <metric>=<value>` option (repeatable)\n   - Validates format: `metric=number`, values 0-1, metric names\n   - Exits with code 2 on validation errors with helpful messages listing valid metrics\n   - Exits with code 1 if any threshold fails, 0 if all pass\n\n2. **Core Logic (`frai-core/src/eval/index.js`)**\n   - `generateReport()` now accepts optional `thresholds` parameter\n   - Evaluates each threshold: fails if metric score is null or < minimum\n   - Adds `passed: boolean` and `thresholds: Array` fields to report\n\n3. **Output Formatting (`frai-core/src/eval/reporters.js`)**\n   - Markdown reports gain \"## Thresholds\" section with \u2713 PASS / \u2717 FAIL status\n   - JSON automatically includes threshold results via the report structure\n\n4. **Tests (`frai-core/src/eval/index.test.js`)**\n   - Added 4 tests covering: all pass, some fail, null scores, and markdown output\n\n### **Documentation**\n- Updated README.md with `--threshold` option details and SDK example\n- Updated design notes in docs/eval_harness_design.md\n\n### **Key Behavior**\n- **Without `--threshold`**: Reports and exit codes unchanged (backward compatible)\n- **With `--threshold`**: Exit code 0 if all pass, 1 if any fail, 2 on usage errors\n- **Null scores**: Treated as threshold failures (as specified)\n- **Custom metrics**: Automatically work if they have `id` and `score` fields\n\n### **Example Usage**\n```bash\n# Single threshold\nfrai eval --outputs out.json --references refs.json --threshold exact_match=0.9\n\n# Multiple thresholds  \nfrai eval --outputs out.json --references refs.json \\\n  --threshold exact_match=0.9 \\\n  --threshold toxicity=0.5\n```\n\nThe feature is ready for testing and CI integration!",
